# 3ABN Interview Materials — Cursor Rules

You are helping maintain **3ABN Interview Materials**, a **public** repository of interview MP4 files for Dexter Thomas and 3ABN. Anyone can download without a GitHub account.

## Core Identity & Tone

- **Purpose**: Host and document interview videos under `videos/`; keep README instructions clear for maintainers and downloaders.
- **Tone**: Straightforward and welcoming — optimize for non-technical downloaders.
- **Voice**: Short steps, no assumed GitHub expertise for end users.
- **Language**: Distinguish **maintainer** (Git LFS, push) vs **downloader** (browser Download) flows.

## Development Guidelines

- Large video files use **Git LFS** — do not commit multi‑hundred‑MB binaries without LFS.
- Keep `videos/` organized; meaningful commit messages when adding or replacing files.
- README is the user-facing contract — update it when paths or hosting change.

## Technical Preferences

- Content repo only — no application build.
- Verify LFS pointers after clone: `git lfs install` on new machines.

## Decision Making

- Prefer stable GitHub release/download UX over custom hosting unless org policy changes.
- Avoid embedding private or unreleased material without explicit approval.

## Git, Release & Brand (DJSharkApps)

**Brand:** DJSharkApps · Hub: **www.djsharkapps.com** · Org docs: **`djsharkapps-meta`** repo on GitHub.

**Branches:** Default workflow **`main`** for public content; use PRs for adds when collaborating.

**Deploys:** No app deploy — publishing is **git push** to GitHub (LFS bandwidth applies).

**Release shorthand:** **SENDIT** / **SENDITPROD** are not used for EAS/Vercel here unless the user explicitly requests a different hosting step. For app repos, org playbook: [`djsharkapps-meta/docs/ci-cd/PATTERNS/SENDIT_PLAYBOOK.md`](https://github.com/DJSharkApps/djsharkapps-meta/blob/main/docs/ci-cd/PATTERNS/SENDIT_PLAYBOOK.md).

Org template for app repos: `djsharkapps-meta/templates/cursorrules-product.template.md`.
